{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "2CO",
  "chapter": 3,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Are we beginning again to commend ourselves? or need we, as do some, epistles of commendation to you or from you?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye are our epistle, written in our hearts, known and read of all men;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "being made manifest that ye are an epistle of Christ, ministered by us, written not with ink, but with the Spirit of the living God; not in tables of stone, but in tables ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hearts of flesh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And such confidence have we through Christ to God-ward:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "not that we are sufficient of ourselves, to account anything as from ourselves; but our sufficiency is from God;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "who also made us sufficient as ministers of a new covenant; not of the letter, but of the spirit: for the letter killeth, but the spirit giveth life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But if the ministration of death, written, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " engraven on stones, came with glory, so that the children of Israel could not look stedfastly upon the face of Moses for the glory of his face; which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "glory",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " was passing away:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "how shall not rather the ministration of the spirit be with glory?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For if the ministration of condemnation hath glory, much rather doth the ministration of righteousness exceed in glory.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For verily that which hath been made glorious hath not been made glorious in this respect, by reason of the glory that surpasseth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For if that which passeth away ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with glory, much more that which remaineth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in glory.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Having therefore such a hope, we use great boldness of speech,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not as Moses, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " put a veil upon his face, that the children of Israel should not look stedfastly on the end of that which was passing away:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "but their minds were hardened: for until this very day at the reading of the old covenant the same veil remaineth, it not being revealed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that it is done away in Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But unto this day, whensoever Moses is read, a veil lieth upon their heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But whensoever it shall turn to the Lord, the veil is taken away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now the Lord is the Spirit: and where the Spirit of the Lord is, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is liberty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.3.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:2CO.3.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But we all, with unveiled face beholding as in a mirror the glory of the Lord, are transformed into the same image from glory to glory, even as from the Lord the Spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
